==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|verb}} {{enPR|rĭfŭnd'}}, {{IPA|/rɪˈfʌnd/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|en-us-refund-verb.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}
* {{a|noun}} {{enPR|rē'fŭnd'}}, {{IPA|/ˈriːfʌnd/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|en-us-refund-noun.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|ʌnd|lang=en}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fro|en}} {{m|fro|refunder||restore}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|refundere}}; prefix {{m|la|re-||re-}} + {{m|la|fundere||to pour}}: compare {{etyl|fr|-}} {{m|fr|refondre}}, {{m|fr|refonder}}. See {{m|en|fuse||to melt}}, and compare {{m|en|refound||to cast again}}, and {{m|en|refuse}}.

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{label|en|transitive}} To return ([[money]]) to (someone); to [[reimburse]].
#: ''A governor, that had pillaged the people, was {{...}} sentenced to '''refund''' what he had wrongfully taken.'' &mdash; L'Estrange.
#: ''If you find this computer for sale anywhere at a lower price, we'll refund you the difference.''
# {{label|en|obsolete}} To [[supply]] again with funds.
#: ''to '''refund''' a railroad loan''
# {{label|en|obsolete|rare}} To [[pour]] back.
#: ''Were the humours of the eye tinctured with any colour, they would '''refund''' that colour upon the object.'' &mdash; Ray.

